    "body": "## Problem\n\nOn the web app, video thumbnails in the profile grid (and likely other feeds) don't support standard browser behaviors:\n\n- Middle-click / scroll-wheel-click doesn't open the video in a new tab\n- Right-click → \\\"Open in new tab\\\" isn't offered\n\nThis blocks a common power-user workflow — opening several videos into background tabs to review them without losing scroll position in the source feed. A moderator triaging a creator's catalog hit this directly.\n\n## Expected\n\nThumbnails behave like native links: middle-click and right-click → \\\"Open link in new tab\\\" both work.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Likely cause: thumbnails are clickable `<div>`/`<button>`s with `onClick` navigation instead of real `<a href>` elements. Switching to anchor-based navigation (or wrapping the clickable area in `<a>`) restores native browser behavior for free.\n- Audit other feed surfaces (home, trending, search results) for the same pattern while we're in there.",
