    "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen a user scrolls deep into a profile's video grid, clicks a video to open it, then navigates back, the grid resets to the top. The user has to re-scroll and the feed re-fetches from page 1.\n\nThis is especially painful for moderators triaging a creator's catalog — they lose their place every time they open a video to report it.\n\n## Expected\n\nReturning to the profile page should restore the previous scroll position and the videos that were already loaded, without re-fetching from the start.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Likely needs scroll restoration on the profile videos route and cache preservation of the loaded pages (TanStack Query `gcTime` may already cover the data; the missing piece is scroll position + which pages were loaded).\n- Related: if thumbnails were real `<a href>` links, users could middle-click to open in a new tab and sidestep the problem entirely (filed separately).",
